      "visualHeaderTooltip": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "text": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'Key findings. 1. Combining five models gives the lowest error at 1 day and 1 week; at 1 month HAR-X alone is best. 2. Beyond HAR-X the algorithm matters little: at 1 week LightGBM, LSTM and Transformer cannot be told apart from HAR-X statistically (Diebold-Mariano tests) and only the combinations beat it; at 1 day they all beat it, but by 2% at most. 3. The Transformer has the lowest average error (MAE) at 1 week and 1 month and is among the best in calm markets, but falls behind in crises: it reacts late when volatility jumps, which QLIKE punishes and MAE does not. 4. For risk limits, any volatility model beats historical simulation: with a multiplier learned from the data, the 99% VaR is violated on 1.1-1.2% of days (target 1%).'"
                }
              }
            },
            "fontSize": {
